Sure, "give" can be used with prepositions. I was pointing it out as an
example where an English word has 3 places without the need for
prepositions. The fact that you *can *use prepositions is orthogonal to
this fact.

By the way, a neat thing I learned about recently:
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V2_word_order
In short, this "the subject is always at least before, if not immediately
before, the verb" rule is unique to English among Germanic languages.

